{"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SegmentSpecBatchEncoder","kind":"identifier"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Make the destination with one of the factories, which fill in the endpoint, the credentials’","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"header field, this encoder and its limits:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/segment(writeKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/rudderStack(writeKey:dataPlane:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/documentation\/SegmentSpecEncoding\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/customerIO(apiKey:region:plan:backoff:clock:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":":","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let segment = try HTTPDestination.segment(","    writeKey: writeKey,","    region: .us,  \/\/ or .eu, where the workspace is","    plan: plan)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The body is a JSON object of content type ","type":"text"},{"code":"application\/json","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with one member, ","type":"text"},{"code":"batch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", an array","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of track calls, one per record, oldest first, with these members:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Member"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Holds"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"anonymousId","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s session, its ","type":"text"},{"code":"SessionKey","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as a lowercase UUID string; the record’s own ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when its context has no session","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The standard context, in the spec’s field names (below), and ","type":"text"},{"code":"ip","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"0.0.0.0\"","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"event","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The event’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Event\/name"},{"type":"text","text":", as it is"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"messageId"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The record’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"EventRecord\/id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", as a lowercase UUID string; a redelivered record keeps it","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"properties"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The event’s stored properties, by name","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"request_ip"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"0.0.0.0\""},{"type":"text","text":", in RudderStack’s calls alone"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"timestamp","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"When the event was tracked, in ISO 8601 with milliseconds, in UTC","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"type","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"\"track\"","type":"codeVoice"}]}]]],"header":"row"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The session is the only identifier sent: there is no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"userId"},{"type":"text","text":", no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"identify"},{"type":"text","text":" call, no traits,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context.device.id"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"advertisingId"},{"type":"text","text":". An endpoint counts a user per "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anonymousId"},{"type":"text","text":", so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its anonymous users are sessions. A record with no session (one tracked by a tracker without"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.sessions()"},{"type":"text","text":") is its own anonymous user, linked to nothing: the spec rejects a call"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with neither a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"userId"},{"type":"text","text":" nor an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anonymousId"},{"type":"text","text":". A record a store recovers after a relaunch keeps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its session, so it goes out with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anonymousId"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"messageId"},{"type":"text","text":" of its first send. Segment"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deduplicates calls by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"messageId"},{"type":"text","text":" over about the last 24 hours, and drops most duplicates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rather than all, so a recovered record Segment had already stored before the app ended is most"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"likely not stored again. RudderStack’s and Customer.io’s references don’t say whether they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"deduplicate. The record’s vendor identifier"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and trace context, and any other context value, aren’t sent."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context.ip"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"0.0.0.0\""},{"text":" in every call, which the spec reads as the user’s address, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Segment records no address from the request. RudderStack fills in a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"request_ip"},{"text":" member from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the request unless the call has one, even when ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context.ip"},{"text":" is set, and passes it on to its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"destinations, so RudderStack’s calls also carry ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"request_ip"},{"text":" as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"0.0.0.0\""},{"text":". Customer.io’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"references don’t say whether ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"context.ip"},{"text":" takes the place of the address it reads from an HTTP","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"request. No call to Segment or Customer.io carries ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"request_ip"},{"text":", which their specs don’t have.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"No ","type":"text"},{"code":"sentAt","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"originalTimestamp","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"channel","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is sent. Without ","type":"text"},{"code":"sentAt","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the endpoint takes","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"timestamp","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as it is, uncorrected for the device’s clock; it is left out on purpose, as a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"retried request sends the same body again, whose ","type":"text"},{"code":"sentAt","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" would be the first attempt’s.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"RudderStack, whose references list all three as required, fills them in from when it received","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the call.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Properties are read through the event’s schema in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"plan"},{"type":"text","text":", as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyReader"},{"type":"text","text":" reads them. A"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Events\/documentation\/Events\/Sensitive","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" value is never sent, whatever the record reveals: the property is left"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"out, an element of an array is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":", and one inside a type the plan can’t map is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"context","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" holds these members, for each of the keys the record’s context has a value for:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"table","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Member","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Key","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Holds","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"app","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ApplicationKey"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"namespace","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the bundle identifier, ","type":"text"},{"code":"version","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"build","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", each left out when ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; no ","type":"text"},{"code":"app","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when all three are","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"device","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DeviceKey"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"model","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the platform as Segment’s Swift library names it: ","type":"text"},{"code":"ios","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a phone or pad, ","type":"text"},{"code":"macos","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"tvos","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"watchos","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"visionos","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"locale"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"LocaleKey","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The locale’s BCP 47 identifier, such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"en-US"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"network","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NetworkKey"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"wifi","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"cellular","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", whether the connection is each"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"os","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent